WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.901
This chapter asks a specific question: After a command contract is

2
00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:08.862
accepted, the stack must choose which obligations become work,

3
00:00:08.862 --> 00:00:13.704
which alternatives remain candidates, what dependencies and observations make nodes feasible,

4
00:00:13.704 --> 00:00:17.665
how scarce capacity is scheduled, when dispatch is permitted,

5
00:00:18.005 --> 00:00:21.260
and how feedback changes only the affected future.

6
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.742
A graph can be acyclic and still pursue the wrong decomposition,

7
00:00:26.742 --> 00:00:30.950
conceal uncertainty, request impossible context, select an inadequate route,

8
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:36.092
violate authority or rights, erase counterfactuals, or create more coordination and

9
00:00:36.092 --> 00:00:38.430
recovery cost than useful work.

10
00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.671
The chapter's core claim is this: Planning as a Control Layer

11
00:00:43.671 --> 00:00:48.313
should own a versioned, consumer-relative plan policy that selects and revises

12
00:00:48.313 --> 00:00:52.110
a partial order of obligations under uncertainty before execution.

13
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:58.785
The policy binds the accepted command version; candidate decompositions and explicit

14
00:00:58.785 --> 00:01:03.393
abstention; typed nodes and dependency semantics; assumptions, observations,

15
00:01:03.393 --> 00:01:09.152
predictive-state and error models; context, tool, capability, authority, rights, resource,

16
00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:10.880
and verifier requirements;

17
00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:16.694
adequacy and utility predicates; lifecycle, dispatch, merge, stop, fallback, recovery,

18
00:01:16.694 --> 00:01:21.073
and replan rules; complete alternative and attempt denominators;

19
00:01:21.073 --> 00:01:26.000
and expected versus observed cost, latency, risk, and residuals.

20
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.630
A concrete implementation trace makes the proposal testable.

21
00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:36.732
The current minimum is a record-and-route scaffold: plan-graph, PlanForge-DAG, command, job,

22
00:01:36.732 --> 00:01:41.969
and semantic-atom schemas; three valid and ten invalid plan-execution fixtures;

23
00:01:41.969 --> 00:01:46.160
two valid scheduler-state traces and seven rejecting mutations;

24
00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.350
two valid runtime-replan traces and nine rejecting mutations;

25
00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:56.681
two accepted no-change transitions; and 33 theorem declarations grouped under seven

26
00:01:56.681 --> 00:01:57.770
manifest targets.

27
00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:04.132
These artifacts exercise exact record shapes, declared dependency order and cycles,

28
00:02:04.132 --> 00:02:09.607
selected lifecycle and dispatch routes, authority/stop preservation bits, local-repair scope,

29
00:02:09.607 --> 00:02:13.440
cost-ledger fields, digests, and no-promotion boundaries only.

30
00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:19.069
They contain no planner-generated natural plan, independent decomposition oracle,

31
00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:24.359
measured dependency truth, context-demand prediction, selected-tier adequacy, live scheduler,

32
00:02:24.359 --> 00:02:27.885
observed replan benefit, or support movement.

33
00:02:28.485 --> 00:02:33.923
The design can still fail. Scope and obligation drift adds goals,

34
00:02:33.923 --> 00:02:39.361
means, parties, or success criteria that the accepted contract did not

35
00:02:39.361 --> 00:02:44.304
authorize. Decomposition theater produces plausible nodes that omit cross-cutting obligations,

36
00:02:44.304 --> 00:02:47.765
irreversible effects, verification, delivery, or recovery work.

37
00:02:48.105 --> 00:02:53.224
Dependency hallucination asserts causal or feasibility relations from textual order,

38
00:02:53.224 --> 00:02:58.856
model confidence, or graph convenience without evidence. Dependency omission allows a

39
00:02:58.856 --> 00:03:04.487
node to dispatch before required data, state, authority, rights, evidence, resource,

40
00:03:04.487 --> 00:03:06.535
or recovery prerequisites exist.

41
00:03:06.875 --> 00:03:10.844
The correct response is to stop, narrow, quarantine, compensate,

42
00:03:10.844 --> 00:03:15.255
or retain an owned residual rather than narrate uncertainty away.

43
00:03:15.855 --> 00:03:20.901
This chapter remains Design rationale at argument support. Its contracts, examples,

44
00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:25.030
tests, or local artifacts establish only their encoded scope.

45
00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:30.076
The chapter names proof targets rather than pretending they are already

46
00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:30.535
closed.

47
00:03:30.875 --> 00:03:35.552
A plan node inherits the authority ceiling of its parent contract

48
00:03:35.552 --> 00:03:40.230
unless governance lowers it. A plan with unsatisfied required constraints cannot

49
00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.080
be dispatched.

50
00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:48.552
Modeled plan-graph admission routes missing command-contract acceptance, decomposition, acyclicity, dependency order,

51
00:03:48.552 --> 00:03:55.035
authority inheritance, context demand, adequacy contracts, verification plans, dispatch gates,

52
00:03:55.035 --> 00:03:58.925
dispatch receipts, replanning controls, residual registers,

53
00:03:59.265 --> 00:04:02.320
and non-claim boundaries to explicit outcomes.

54
00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:07.884
No chapter claim or evidence state is promoted by this visual.

55
00:04:07.884 --> 00:04:12.848
A named mechanism is not proof of correct implementation or useful

56
00:04:12.848 --> 00:04:17.812
deployment. A local check or formal model does not establish real-world

57
00:04:17.812 --> 00:04:22.325
enforcement. No safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI, or ASI conclusion follows.

58
00:04:22.665 --> 00:04:27.140
These boundaries matter because an explanatory derivative is useful only if

59
00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:30.395
it preserves the evidence ceiling of its source.

60
00:04:30.995 --> 00:04:36.157
At most, this visual explains the chapter's design rationale at argument

61
00:04:36.157 --> 00:04:40.850
support; it adds no empirical, deployment, safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI,

62
00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:46.011
or ASI result. The next chapter is Governed World Models and

63
00:04:46.011 --> 00:04:46.950
Reality Grounding.

64
00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:51.684
It takes responsibility for Planning and control fail when an agent's

65
00:04:51.684 --> 00:04:55.278
latent or simulated future is mistaken for the world,

66
00:04:55.278 --> 00:04:59.672
when prediction error is hidden, or when model updates expand action

67
00:04:59.672 --> 00:05:00.870
authority without evidence.
